            <ArticleTitle>Effects of quinapril on coronary blood flow in coronary artery disease patients with endothelial dysfunction. TREND Investigators. Trial on Reversing Endothelial Dysfunction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1594-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This pilot study evaluates the effects of quinapril, an angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitor with high tissue-binding affinity, on microvascular endothelial function in patients with mild (&lt;40% narrowing) coronary artery disease and epicardial endothelial dysfunction. Patients randomized to quinapril had a trend suggesting an increase in endothelium-dependent coronary blood flow response.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
